                                                                <p dir=3D"l=
tr"><span>This tutorial will create a Music Playlist App using the MERN (Mo=
ngoDB, Express.js, React.js, Node.js) stack. The app allows users to manage=
 playlists, add songs, and play their favorite tracks. We'll cover front an=
d backend development, integrating features like song uploading, playlist c=
reation, and playback functionality.</span></p>

<p dir=3D"ltr"><b><strong>Output Preview: </strong></b><span>Let us have a =
look at how the final output will look like.</span></p>

<p dir=3D"ltr"><img alt=3D"imresizer-1710245089584" height=3D"600" src=3D"h=
ttps://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240312173505/imresizer-=
1710245089584.jpg" width=3D"1100"></p>

<h2><span>Prerequisites</span></h2><ul><li value=3D"1"><a href=3D"https://w=
ww.geeksforgeeks.org/node-js-npm-node-package-manager/" rel=3D"noopener" ta=
rget=3D"_blank"><span>Node.js and npm</span></a></li><li value=3D"2"><a hre=
f=3D"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/what-is-mongodb-working-and-features/" r=
el=3D"noopener" target=3D"_blank"><span>MongoDB</span></a></li><li value=3D=
"3"><a href=3D"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/express-js/" rel=3D"noopener" =
target=3D"_blank"><span>Express.js</span></a></li><li value=3D"4"><a href=
=3D"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/reactjs-introduction/" rel=3D"noopener" t=
arget=3D"_blank"><span>React.js</span></a></li><li value=3D"5"><a href=3D"h=
ttps://www.geeksforgeeks.org/how-to-make-get-call-to-an-api-using-axios-in-=
javascript/" rel=3D"noopener" target=3D"_blank"><span>Axios for API request=
s</span></a></li><li value=3D"6"><a href=3D"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/h=
ow-to-handle-file-upload-in-node-with-multer-and-postman/" rel=3D"noopener"=
 target=3D"_blank"><span>Multer for file uploading</span></a></li><li value=
=3D"7"><span>GridFS for storing audio files in MongoDB</span></li></ul><h2>=
<span>Approach to create Music Playlist App:</span></h2><ul><li value=3D"1"=
><span>Create a Node.js project with Express.js.</span></li><li value=3D"2"=
><span>Connect to MongoDB using mongoose.</span></li><li value=3D"3"><span>=
Implement RESTful API endpoints for managing playlists and songs.</span></l=
i><li value=3D"4"><span>Initialize a React.js project.</span></li><li value=
=3D"5"><span>Design components to display playlists and songs.</span></li><=
li value=3D"6"><span>Use Axios to fetch data from the backend and handle us=
er interactions.</span></li><li value=3D"7"><span>Implement file upload fun=
ctionality using Multer and GridFS.</span></li><li value=3D"8"><span>Apply =
CSS to style the app and make it visually appealing.</span></li></ul><h2><s=
pan>Steps to Create the BackEnd:</span></h2><p dir=3D"ltr"><b><strong>Step =
1: </strong></b><span>Set Up Backend Server using following commands:-</spa=
n></p>

<pre><span>mkdir music-playlist-app-backend</span><br><span>cd  music-playl=
ist-app-backend</span><br><span>npm init -y</span><br></pre><p dir=3D"ltr">=
<b><strong>Step 2:</strong></b><span> Install all the necessary dependencie=
s:-</span></p><div id=3D"GFG_AD_Desktop_InContent_ATF_728x280" style=3D"tex=
t-align: center; margin: 10px 0px;"></div>

<pre><span>npm install express mongoose cors multer multer-gridfs-storage</=
span><br></pre><h2><span>Project Structure(Backend):</span></h2><p dir=3D"l=
tr"><img alt=3D"Screenshot-2024-03-12-173020" height=3D"157" loading=3D"laz=
y" src=3D"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240312173038=
